+"""Probe an EXECUTE-lane model's two-turn tool-call entitlement against an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
 
-Why this exists (FAR F-023-A): an execute lane must establish, before a long run, that the model it
-is about to drive can actually complete a multi-turn tool-call conversation through the configured
-endpoint. A prior round lost a run to an adapter defect (D-03/D-04): the upstream provider returns
-``400 invalid_request_error`` on the second turn because the ``reasoning_content`` of the first
-turn's thinking mode was not echoed back to the API. The probe reproduces that class in two turns
-and records it as a TYPED reason instead of a retry loop.
+Why this exists: a long governed run can die on the SECOND provider turn with
+``Provider error 400: Upstream request failed: [invalid_request_error] The `reasoning_content` in
+the thinking mode must be passed back to the API.`` The run then fails *after* doing work. This probe
+asks the endpoint for a tool call on turn 1 and continues that same conversation on turn 2, so the
+entitlement is established BEFORE the long run and recorded as a receipt carrying the DECLARED and
+the OBSERVED model (a substitution is disclosed, never silent).
 
